-- title:
--   Galois-stable divisors have K-rational symmetric coefficients
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \ge 1$ and an intermediate field $K$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ (no finiteness over $\mathbb{Q}$ is assumed), together with a natural number $g'$. Let $D$ be a divisor of the field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,N$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, that is, a finitely supported $\mathbb{Z}$-valued function on the set of places of the extension $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \subset \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,N$, a place being a valuation subring that contains the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, is not the whole field, and is a principal ideal ring; here $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,N$ is the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the coefficientwise image of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,N$, the latter being $\mathbb{Q}$ adjoined the $q$-expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,d\,jq$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $N$. Assume $D$ is invariant: for every $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ lying in the fixing subgroup of $K$, the semilinear automorphism $\mathrm{arithmeticGalois}\,(\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,N)\,\sigma$ — the pair consisting of $\sigma$ and of the coefficientwise action of $\sigma$ on Laurent series, restricted to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,N$ — acts on divisors so as to send $D$ to itself. The conclusion is that for each $k \in \{0,\dots,g'\}$ the value $\mathrm{symVec}\,N\,g'\,D\,k$, namely the coefficient of $X^{g'-k}$ (truncated subtraction) of the polynomial $\prod_{v} (\mathrm{jFactor}\,N\,v)^{\max(D(v),0)}$ over the support of $D$, lies in $K$.
--
--   This is the $K$-rationality of the elementary symmetric functions of the $j$-coordinates of a divisor that is rational over $K$: a Galois element fixing $K$ permutes the places occurring in $D$ with their multiplicities, so the coefficients of the associated monic product are $K$-rational. It is used in the naive-height estimates for divisor classes on $J_0(N)$, where heights are computed from the vector $\mathrm{symVec}\,N\,g'\,D$ of a chosen representative divisor.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_symVec_mem_of_stable.lean

import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_JZeroNaiveHeight
